## 3 · 🌉 THE GATE — other Mente OS instances

Other projects have their own Mente OS (declare yours below). This one **points at them but does
not integrate them** — integrating burns tokens with no request behind it.

| | |
|---|---|
| ⛔ **Never read** another project's Mente OS without the owner using the access phrase | not "for context", not "just in case" |
| **Open** | the owner writes `acceder mente <project>` → confirm the WHY → **read-only + report** |
| **Close** | `cerrar mente <project>` **or** auto-close when the task ends, whichever comes first |
| **Enforcement** | 🔒 `deny` on Read/Edit/Write in **both** `.claude/settings.json` and `settings.local.json` |

⭐ **The gate is a technical lock, not a promise.** It was doctrine once, and got violated
6 times in one session. Now the harness refuses. **Never propose lifting a deny for convenience.**

Registry and full rules: `Mente/connection/bridges/`.

